criteria.update({'status':'proposed; coordinator must reconcile and freeze into brief.qualityCriteria before candidate submission','judgment':'Compare actual native exports to fixed target, source, and approved native family. Reward useful modeling improvements. No arbitrary aesthetic numerical pass threshold; no prescribed cosmetic implementation. Missing required evidence means needs_evidence.','aestheticOutcomes':[{'id':'shape-volume','outcome':'Quarter turn remains recognizable and feels like substantial crafted conveyor construction. Outer and inner rails, deck and supporting wood have clear, coherent volume in all4facings; purposeful native design improvements are rewarded within functional envelope.'},{'id':'color-family','outcome':'Warm coral rail, cool blue-gray deck and warm honey/brown support form a clear palette hierarchy. Exact approved family connection planes match; curved interior belongs to the same family without muddy, nearly black wood or excessive orange saturation.'},{'id':'soft-light','outcome':'Broad soft light and restrained stable highlights separate top/side forms and preserve warm lower-face readability. No horizontal directional bias, cast ground shadow, blown highlight stripe, noisy/glittering shading or unmotivated black patch.'},{'id':'materials-detail','outcome':'Wood, rail and moving deck read as different purposeful materials. Crafted details support the form, remain stable in motion, and survive representative intended sizes where useful; tiny target marks, exact bolt count, old part count and old weak geometry are not mandatory.'},{'id':'readability','outcome':'The turning route, moving deck, outer/inner rail separation and supporting mass remain clear at cell128,55,32 and a fractional pitch, including phone-sized current consumer views and contrasting backgrounds.'},{'id':'deadspot-free','outcome':'No materially distracting seam, open black hole, coplanar flicker, disconnected or floating support, clipped form, alpha halo, overhanging connector, support-to-deck intrusion, abrupt normal discontinuity or merged muddy mass in any required facing/frame.'},{'id':'motion-and-modular','outcome':'Deck bands visibly travel E-to-N with the original fanned law and synchronized7-period2second loop; rail/wood remain stationary. Both joins to approved directional straights remain continuous in shape, color, highlight, coverage and temporal phase, including loop wrap and fractional sampling.'}], 'immutableContract':{'capture':{'frame':[384,704],'logicalFrame':[192,352],'logicalRoot':[96,248],'rootPixels':[192,496],'sourceScale':2,'cellSize':128,'pixelAspect':[1.2206555604934692,1],'camera':'Exact approved family registered camera in inputs/family-settings.json, calibrated256px/unit at publication2x. Single common camera/material/light configuration, root rotation only for facings. No target-derived fitting/warp/painting/card and no per-facing recolor.','rootRotationsDegrees':{'N':180,'E':90,'S':0,'W':-90},'intrinsicOrientationRadians':0},'roleAndEnvelope':{'footprint':[1,1],'groundZ':0,'sourceBounds':[[-.48,-.48,0],[.5,.5,.695]],'functionalHeight':.695,'deckHeight':.64,'deckSocket':[0,0,.64],'policy':'Keep registered footprint, original turning deck path, usable deck clearance, actual ports and ground contact. Nonfunctional support design, topology, decoration and part counts may change within this contract.'},'portsRootS':{'incoming':{'plane':'X=.5','center':[.5,0,.64],'travelTangent':[-1,0,0],'deckSpanTransverse':[-.35,.35],'UV':0},'outgoing':{'plane':'Y=.5','center':[0,.5,.64],'travelTangent':[0,1,0],'deckSpanTransverse':[-.35,.35],'UV':1},'railCrossSection':{'transverseSpans':[[-.48,-.35],[.35,.48]],'zSpan':[.505,.695]},'family':'Exact approved native family settings599d7a731dcf8f22305f3d7b8a67a1fa45743535ed34937620dd9a834377ba15; native projectd210743fdff9c17e393d4d2ca59e61c9ea1d5819c2952c10ea40f29b21ff0328. Open terminal profiles and rail/deck radiance/material coordinates must remain continuous. Equivalent native curved cross-section coordinate basis is necessary; arbitrary worldX mapping does not establish continuity.'},'deckAndMotion':{'centerXY':[.5,.5],'radii':[.15,.85],'angularLaw':'theta=pi+(pi/2)*q','U':'1-[(pi/4)*q+(1-pi/4)*(3*q*q-2*q*q*q)]','V':'0inner1outer','phase':'-7*i/24, i0..24','running':{'uniqueFrames':24,'fps':12,'seconds':2,'closureNativeFrame':25,'atlasColumns':6,'atlasRows':4,'atlasSize':[2304,2816]},'note':'Preserve true directed action and UV law independently of geometry tessellation; not12frames, constant angular speed, straight tangent translation, or opposite handedness.'},'exclusions':['No editing other objects, production outputs, target, brief, backups, or the3excluded restaurant floor designs.','No unrelated gameplay changes required for this asset.']},'candidateEvidence':{'nativeAndPortable':['Immutable hash-bound packet with exact editable.blend, recipe/settings, full dependencies and resource closure. Reopen saved bytes in a render-only replay without hidden authoring callbacks; exact source/render provenance required.','All96unique native384x704 frames (4facings×24) plus4frame25 closure renders; exact original-layout24frame atlases. Labelled contact sheets may index every frame without adding unnecessary larger captures.','Actual12fps playback of all4facings and mixed joins covering at least2full loops; inspect23→0 wrap, stationary rail/wood and deck-band motion. GIF/WebP/video/frame trace must use declared24frame timing, not hand-selected static frames.','Compact actual native audit: registered camera matrices/projection/pixel aspect/calibration; root and intrinsic transform; evaluated geometry bounds/ground/clearance; measured terminal rings/profiles/tangents; UV endpoint/interior samples and actual bound phase keys including closure; exact family project/settings hashes. Old metadata and unrelated active source camera are not proof.'], 'modularContinuity':['Show genuine native mixed incoming-straight + this-corner + outgoing-straight at one-cell root offsets, with correct compatible native family direction/phase, in all4rotations. Inspect both joins. Do not substitute a repeated straight-only strip, two corners of the wrong hand, or target-based alpha fitting.','Supply an actual native unbroken connected reference with equivalent family construction and the corner curved coordinate law, and independently assemble the exact proposed published sprites at registered roots. Compare at all24phases using compact contact/loop evidence; preserve source materials/UV coordinates in the reference so changed procedural Object coordinates do not invalidate the comparison.','Provide fullRGBA residual maps plus per-joinROI RGB/alpha localization for assembled versus native-unbroken reference. Report position and extent of differences, not only averages/alpha maxima. If smooth curve-interior normal or geometric variation creates valid residuals, identify it and visually substantiate it; no visible join stripe, hole, coverage doubling or temporal discontinuity may be concealed by overall averages.'], 'currentConsumers':['Use actual current SpriteScene/world-sprite-raster (ready=true plus painted frame) and actual current Godot native compositor for bounded corner fixtures. Verify dependencies by paths/hashes; no surrogate bilinear renderer or claimed test of an unrun consumer.','Representative all4facing mixed joins at128,55,32 and one fractionalcell pitch such as47.3. Include integer and subpixel camera/grid origins, light/gray/dark/transparent surfaces, frame0 and representative motion phases, plus12fps wrap playback. Keep large matrices proportionate: full native100frame audit is mandatory; small consumer grids may use representative phases if actual24frame motion loops and residual coverage establish joins.','Inspect at actual intended display scale and enlarged join crops, with a phone390x844 or equivalent current SpriteScene view. Distinguish texture/sprite compatibility from gameplay: current restaurant_view only picks start/straight/end and linear dish travel; a new corner routing/simulation feature and unrelated fullgame artifacts are outside this review.']},'reviewPolicy':{'roundVerdict':'approve only if visible improvement toward fixed style and no material defects, while all technical and evidence requirements pass; otherwise revise or needs_evidence','blockers':'At most3 ranked outcome blockers per round; describe visible effect/location and desired outcome, not the cosmetic method.','remainingDifferences':'Accept coherent native interpretation and useful design improvements; exact target pixel identity or copying target framing/endcaps is not required.','scores':'Comparative observations only if useful; no universal or arbitrary aesthetic pass score.'},'reconciliationNeeded':initial['reconciliationNeededBeforeEditor']})
